1
00:00:01,961 --> 00:00:04,755
I was asleep for like two hours.

2
00:00:05,297 --> 00:00:06,924
Two hours is pretty intense.

3
00:00:07,591 --> 00:00:10,094
Got some real sleep on the couch.

4
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:12,847
I woke up with a total jolt.

5
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:15,349
How'd it go?

6
00:00:16,308 --> 00:00:18,519
The jacuzzi? How'd it go?

7
00:00:21,397 --> 00:00:26,152
I felt like a lot's shifted since
coming here. Everyone's changing.

8
00:00:26,819 --> 00:00:30,030
Why are you dishing it out piece by piece?

9
00:00:31,866 --> 00:00:34,535
Maybe he's finally moved past it.

10
00:00:37,413 --> 00:00:39,123
Maybe I pushed him too much.

11
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:41,751
You didn't expect that?

12
00:00:43,419 --> 00:00:44,378
I did.

13
00:00:44,462 --> 00:00:45,546
You did?

14
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:47,715
But he'd never say that to my face.

15
00:00:49,508 --> 00:00:51,969
Maybe he's just accepted it.

16
00:00:56,098 --> 00:00:58,184
Like, this is just painful.

17
00:01:03,314 --> 00:01:05,065
If you had to sum up

18
00:01:05,149 --> 00:01:07,526
this hocance in one single kanji,
what would it be?

19
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:09,528
I wanna ask everyone.

20
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:12,698
They throw in random prompts sometimes.

21
00:01:12,782 --> 00:01:15,284
Feels like something the writers
cooked up.

22
00:01:16,327 --> 00:01:18,412
"Fun."

23
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:22,833
I'm jealous.

24
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,587
Jealous?

25
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:28,964
How about you, Hiroyoshi?

26
00:01:29,507 --> 00:01:30,549
"Pain."

27
00:01:32,426 --> 00:01:34,845
Care to spell it out?

28
00:01:34,929 --> 00:01:36,555
As in "suffering".

29
00:01:38,015 --> 00:01:39,642
Nothing else fits.

30
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:47,817
Classic me, right?

31
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:50,194
Yeah… Oops, I actually agreed out loud.

32
00:01:50,569 --> 00:01:51,737
What about you, Misato?

33
00:01:51,821 --> 00:01:53,781
Mine's "Booze".

34
00:01:55,366 --> 00:01:57,076
Wasn't it the same last year?

35
00:01:59,954 --> 00:02:01,497
So he's in pain.

36
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:07,169
When it gets like this,
I just lose any desire to talk.

37
00:02:07,253 --> 00:02:09,129
Which part set you off?

38
00:02:10,965 --> 00:02:12,258
The "pain" thing.

39
00:02:13,592 --> 00:02:16,262
Like, he had to say that

40
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:18,138
in front of everyone?

41
00:02:18,222 --> 00:02:21,725
Well, you're the one who kept popping off
in front of everyone.

42
00:02:23,102 --> 00:02:24,395
Really.

43
00:02:30,234 --> 00:02:31,777
I'm awful.

44
00:02:32,111 --> 00:02:33,612
All of a sudden?

45
00:02:33,988 --> 00:02:35,114
Out of nowhere?

46
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:36,657
I'm pretty awful.

47
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:38,200
Which part made you say that?

48
00:02:38,284 --> 00:02:39,118
"Painful."

49
00:02:39,201 --> 00:02:41,203
That he said that?

50
00:02:42,746 --> 00:02:44,248
You weren't conscious?

51
00:02:45,499 --> 00:02:47,918
I mean, I was, but…

52
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:51,672
but the fact that
that was his final takeaway?

53
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:53,924
That's definitely a shock.

54
00:02:54,842 --> 00:02:57,720
Doesn't that just show how hard
he was taking it?

55
00:02:58,888 --> 00:03:00,764
With himself? Or with me?

56
00:03:00,848 --> 00:03:03,726
With himself… and you.

57
00:03:05,019 --> 00:03:06,478
But…

58
00:03:06,562 --> 00:03:10,441
if you're just over it, it's fine, right?

59
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:13,861
You want a love that doesn't wobble.

60
00:03:15,404 --> 00:03:17,364
Maybe she was testing him the whole time.

61
00:03:17,448 --> 00:03:20,659
She probably wanted Hiroyoshi to
keep coming after her no matter what.

62
00:03:23,871 --> 00:03:25,247
What's that sound?

63
00:03:25,623 --> 00:03:27,791
Did someone just meow?

64
00:03:27,917 --> 00:03:28,876
A cat?

65
00:03:28,959 --> 00:03:29,793
The sound.

66
00:03:31,086 --> 00:03:32,713
Must be tired.

67
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:34,173
Tired?

68
00:03:34,256 --> 00:03:36,592
Sorry, am I hearing things?

69
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:38,052
No, no.

70
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,219
Oh, them?

71
00:03:39,303 --> 00:03:40,137
Kaede.

72
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,555
I'm not that mean.

73
00:03:41,639 --> 00:03:43,265
Shut up, shut up.

74
00:03:43,349 --> 00:03:44,850
Come here for a sec.

75
00:03:44,934 --> 00:03:46,018
Me?

76
00:03:46,101 --> 00:03:47,561
What? Scary, scary.

77
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:49,563
Can I steal you away for a second?

78
00:03:49,647 --> 00:03:52,274
Are you mad? Are you pissed off?

79
00:03:52,358 --> 00:03:53,651
Come over here.

80
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:55,861
What, what? I'm scared.

81
00:04:00,616 --> 00:04:02,242
Do I look like I'm pissed?

82
00:04:02,326 --> 00:04:05,704
I mean, with that vibe, everyone was like,

83
00:04:05,788 --> 00:04:07,539
"What's his deal?"

84
00:04:07,623 --> 00:04:11,085
Everyone keeps saying
I'm all aggressive, right?

85
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:13,796
So I decided to just lean into it.

86
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:16,507
Oh, so that was the play.

87
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:18,634
Then I saw the handkerchief

88
00:04:18,717 --> 00:04:21,720
and was like,
"Since when do you carry one of those?"

89
00:04:22,221 --> 00:04:24,223
Total act, man.

90
00:04:24,306 --> 00:04:27,101
I was legitimately freaked out!

91
00:04:27,476 --> 00:04:28,686
I was like, "Oh, great."

92
00:04:28,769 --> 00:04:31,480
"Here we go again."

93
00:04:31,563 --> 00:04:33,065
But yeah.

94
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:34,525
You know,

95
00:04:34,984 --> 00:04:37,194
we went to the aquarium yesterday, right?

96
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:40,739
And then today, Mao invited me out.

97
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:44,118
I was hyped out of my mind.

98
00:04:44,201 --> 00:04:45,536
Mao told you all, right?

99
00:04:47,913 --> 00:04:49,832
But hey,

100
00:04:49,915 --> 00:04:51,875
yesterday was super fun too, for real.

101
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:55,546
I didn't care about that at all.

102
00:04:55,671 --> 00:04:56,880
Oh, really?

103
00:04:56,964 --> 00:04:59,258
You were just like, "Oh, good for him."

104
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:04,430
Honestly, I was just smiling,

105
00:05:04,513 --> 00:05:06,056
thinking, "that's nice."

106
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,642
"You prefer a wild fish,
not a stray catch, huh."

107
00:05:08,726 --> 00:05:10,519
Were you sitting there

108
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:12,938
thinking something like that?

109
00:05:13,022 --> 00:05:16,150
No, I wasn't thinking that at all.

110
00:05:16,734 --> 00:05:21,321
I just wanted to make sure you knew
I enjoyed the fish date yesterday.

111
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:23,657
You're overthinking this way too much.

112
00:05:23,741 --> 00:05:26,869
Because look,

113
00:05:27,036 --> 00:05:29,413
this could easily turn into

114
00:05:30,247 --> 00:05:32,833
another one of our
classic miscommunications.

115
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:36,962
I wanted to say loud and clear that
I had fun on the fish date.

116
00:05:37,046 --> 00:05:40,883
Even if they're totally different fish,

117
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:43,552
like wild-caught versus farm-raised.

118
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:46,221
Yesterday's farm-raised setup was
still super fun.

119
00:05:46,305 --> 00:05:50,100
I'm not sweating that at all.

120
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:56,398
Just wanted to clear the air.

121
00:05:56,482 --> 00:05:58,067
That's it?

122
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:00,069
Yeah.

123
00:06:00,152 --> 00:06:01,320
Gotcha.

124
00:06:01,403 --> 00:06:04,948
Seriously, don't worry about it.

125
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:11,288
If there's any lingering friction,
I wanna fix it.

126
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:15,876
Even if we end up as just friends,

127
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:19,755
we can't have all this
weird baggage, right?

128
00:06:23,675 --> 00:06:27,054
And if we ever became a couple again,

129
00:06:27,137 --> 00:06:28,555
it'd be ten times worse.

130
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:34,770
I never actually dealt with
any of this in the past,

131
00:06:34,853 --> 00:06:37,856
so I knew I had to face it

132
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,692
head-on,

133
00:06:43,028 --> 00:06:44,738
you know?

134
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:49,159
That's my thought.

135
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:55,624
Honestly though,
seeing how much you've changed…

136
00:06:55,707 --> 00:06:59,837
While I was just sitting here saying
I had zero good memories with you,

137
00:07:01,130 --> 00:07:04,258
stumbling over my words,

138
00:07:04,341 --> 00:07:08,846
constantly whining about
how painful it was.

139
00:07:09,096 --> 00:07:13,767
But you actually listened to
every bit of it.

140
00:07:14,226 --> 00:07:17,521
You owned up to where you messed up,

141
00:07:17,813 --> 00:07:21,233
and after getting called out
by everyone else,

142
00:07:21,316 --> 00:07:23,986
you realized

143
00:07:24,278 --> 00:07:27,573
you needed to change.

144
00:07:27,990 --> 00:07:30,617
I really respect that.

145
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:37,416
I think it's amazing. But even so…

146
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:41,795
I still can't picture us

147
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:46,133
actually being together again.

148
00:07:46,216 --> 00:07:48,677
It's like…
I keep getting these flashbacks.

149
00:07:52,181 --> 00:07:57,686
I want to believe you,

150
00:07:57,769 --> 00:08:01,273
but I just can't bring myself
to take that step.

151
00:08:01,565 --> 00:08:04,026
You've made so much progress,

152
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:06,862
and I feel like I'm the only one stuck

153
00:08:07,321 --> 00:08:08,947
in the past.

154
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:14,995
I do believe you've changed…

155
00:08:16,038 --> 00:08:19,416
but it's my own weakness.

156
00:08:22,878 --> 00:08:25,088
I just can't make that leap of faith.

157
00:08:33,597 --> 00:08:36,934
But it's hard to act like
it never happened.

158
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:39,519
Real change is just so damn hard.

159
00:08:48,403 --> 00:08:50,697
So yeah,

160
00:08:50,781 --> 00:08:53,158
I want to work things out, but…

161
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:03,043
honestly,

162
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:09,549
since you're probably still torn
between Mao and me,

163
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:13,011
I want you to take your time.

164
00:09:22,604 --> 00:09:24,773
Yoko, why the sudden mood shift?

165
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:26,942
What happened to Happy Yoko?

166
00:09:27,526 --> 00:09:29,695
Something unpleasant happened.

167
00:09:30,487 --> 00:09:32,698
Why are they whispering over there?

168
00:09:33,282 --> 00:09:36,618
If he's got something to say,
he can say it to my face.

169
00:09:38,996 --> 00:09:41,790
Like, seriously…
whispering right next to me?

170
00:09:42,374 --> 00:09:43,500
What's his problem?

171
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:47,546
"Whispering right next to each other."

172
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:50,632
They're acting like high schoolers.

173
00:09:50,841 --> 00:09:52,676
"I confronted things head-on,"

174
00:09:52,759 --> 00:09:54,553
"but you refused to meet me halfway."

175
00:09:54,636 --> 00:09:56,972
Why did X come here?
What do you want to do?

176
00:09:57,055 --> 00:09:59,641
I wanted to make it clear today

177
00:09:59,725 --> 00:10:03,603
that I'm totally over it.
Even with X around,

178
00:10:03,687 --> 00:10:05,397
I'm unfazed.

179
00:10:05,689 --> 00:10:08,650
Flipping to "I'm done with this"
in a single day makes

180
00:10:08,734 --> 00:10:09,860
zero sense to me.

181
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:11,194
What is he trying to do?

182
00:10:11,278 --> 00:10:13,488
He thinks I'm ignoring my own issues here?

183
00:10:13,572 --> 00:10:15,574
I'm like, "Is that so?"

184
00:10:15,657 --> 00:10:16,825
Can I just go back to my room?

185
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:18,160
Must be uncomfortable for everyone.

186
00:10:18,243 --> 00:10:19,202
They're just fighting.

187
00:10:19,286 --> 00:10:20,370
Aren't you gonna regret this?

188
00:10:20,454 --> 00:10:22,456
Nope. Being stuck here now is way worse.

189
00:10:22,789 --> 00:10:23,623
Sorry.

190
00:10:23,707 --> 00:10:24,541
It's fine.

191
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:26,376
I can't deal with this.

192
00:10:31,882 --> 00:10:33,258
Oh, my…

193
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:51,276
She grabbed the vase and
went to the bathroom…

194
00:10:55,072 --> 00:10:56,531
Is she… dumping it out?

195
00:10:56,615 --> 00:10:57,908
Wait…

196
00:10:58,784 --> 00:11:00,911
Don't smash it!

197
00:11:01,745 --> 00:11:05,540
Yoko wants all eyes on her.

198
00:11:05,624 --> 00:11:10,003
Her dream scenario is
someone who stays with her

199
00:11:11,213 --> 00:11:14,800
no matter how toxic she acts.

200
00:11:15,801 --> 00:11:18,804
She always seemed
so upbeat on the surface,

201
00:11:18,887 --> 00:11:21,056
but she must have been harboring

202
00:11:21,556 --> 00:11:24,684
some real hurt underneath.

203
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:29,815
Misato's comments really got to me…

204
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:31,733
especially about the two choices.

205
00:11:31,817 --> 00:11:34,986
"Take all the time you need
to figure it out."

206
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:37,239
The way she gently told him.

207
00:11:37,322 --> 00:11:41,034
Her self-esteem took such a huge hit
that she hasn't recovered enough

208
00:11:41,118 --> 00:11:44,162
to be like, "Hey, look at me!"

209
00:11:44,246 --> 00:11:47,916
When you've been around someone like that,

210
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:49,876
those toxic patterns

211
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:52,254
stay deeply rooted even after time apart.

212
00:11:52,671 --> 00:11:54,047
Exactly.

213
00:12:00,929 --> 00:12:03,140
And Hikaru…

214
00:12:03,223 --> 00:12:05,434
right after he had his little sulk.

215
00:12:06,893 --> 00:12:09,396
Hikaru, morning.

216
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:10,397
Oh, is this…?

217
00:12:11,106 --> 00:12:12,357
Mao.

218
00:12:12,441 --> 00:12:13,358
Ignoring her?

219
00:12:14,901 --> 00:12:16,736
That looked like a blatant ignore.

220
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,280
Hikaru.

221
00:12:25,162 --> 00:12:27,497
Hey! Hey!

222
00:12:27,831 --> 00:12:29,291
Silent treatment?

223
00:12:41,553 --> 00:12:43,346
Good morning.

224
00:12:46,475 --> 00:12:47,893
Wanna go on a date?

225
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:51,855
Meet in the lounge at 11.

226
00:12:52,314 --> 00:12:53,940
Lunch at a Ryukyu izakaya.

227
00:12:54,024 --> 00:12:54,858
Nice.

228
00:12:54,983 --> 00:12:55,901
Is casual attire okay?

229
00:12:55,984 --> 00:12:57,235
I'm going like this.

230
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:18,215
I sensed something.

231
00:13:18,715 --> 00:13:20,258
Why aren't you coming over to me?

232
00:13:20,342 --> 00:13:21,510
Why?

233
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:23,595
Me?

234
00:13:25,931 --> 00:13:28,975
Why do I have to be the one
to go over there?

235
00:13:31,686 --> 00:13:34,689
Shoppi, what do you think,
seeing adults like this?

236
00:13:34,773 --> 00:13:37,108
Adults are really just big kids.

237
00:13:37,192 --> 00:13:38,401
Ain't that the truth.

238
00:13:39,194 --> 00:13:41,821
I don't get why you're acting like this.

239
00:13:41,905 --> 00:13:43,281
Why are you mad? What happened?

240
00:13:43,365 --> 00:13:45,492
I'm not mad.

241
00:13:45,575 --> 00:13:46,451
Did I do something?

242
00:13:46,535 --> 00:13:47,410
I'm totally not mad.

243
00:13:47,494 --> 00:13:48,328
You're not?

244
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:50,580
He's acting like a big five-year-old son.

245
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:53,875
Today's the final day!
You don't have time to be sleeping in.

246
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:56,336
What are you gonna do?

247
00:13:56,419 --> 00:13:58,838
I mean,
I already laid my cards on the table.

248
00:13:58,922 --> 00:14:02,342
I told you I wanted an answer

249
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:05,470
to what I asked of you yesterday.

250
00:14:07,806 --> 00:14:10,684
Didn't I say I'd accept what you said?

251
00:14:10,934 --> 00:14:13,478
And you can just swallow all that
so easily?

252
00:14:13,562 --> 00:14:14,688
What?

253
00:14:17,899 --> 00:14:19,734
Does this look easy to you?

254
00:14:20,443 --> 00:14:22,654
That's the thing… like,

255
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:25,574
even right now,
you're seriously gonna hear me out

256
00:14:25,657 --> 00:14:27,450
lying down like that?

257
00:14:29,119 --> 00:14:31,997
Look, I already put
a ton of thought into this,

258
00:14:33,206 --> 00:14:37,377
and what I told you the other day
was my final answer.

259
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:42,632
Does that mean
you're actually ready to own all of it?

260
00:14:42,716 --> 00:14:45,302
I was planning to, yeah.

261
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:49,222
You were planning to? So then, what?

262
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:57,022
Give me specifics.
Like, are you ready to move in together?

263
00:14:57,355 --> 00:14:58,440
We've been living apart.

264
00:14:58,523 --> 00:14:59,441
Me?

265
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:04,946
Like, how much do you intend to earn?

266
00:15:05,030 --> 00:15:07,282
How are we gonna split the bills?

267
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:10,744
Wanting to make money is one thing,
actually pulling it in is another.

268
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:15,540
We have to look at
this stuff realistically, right?

269
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,630
Good morning.

270
00:15:22,714 --> 00:15:24,341
Last morning already?

271
00:15:25,008 --> 00:15:25,925
Our last day.

272
00:15:26,009 --> 00:15:26,968
Last day!

273
00:15:27,052 --> 00:15:28,970
Let's have a great day today!

274
00:15:29,054 --> 00:15:30,472
Yeah!

275
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,733
Honestly,

276
00:15:41,816 --> 00:15:47,197
everything I laid on you…

277
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:51,034
past-you would've just gone, "Wait, what?"

278
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:55,372
It wasn't a surprising moment at all,

279
00:15:57,749 --> 00:15:59,501
to begin with.

280
00:16:02,087 --> 00:16:06,424
I already laid my cards on the table,

281
00:16:06,883 --> 00:16:09,636
so now the ball is in your court.

282
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:12,430
It's up to what you want to do.

283
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:14,391
Ultimately,

284
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:19,646
my next move depends on
how that plays out,

285
00:16:19,938 --> 00:16:21,439
to be blunt.

286
00:16:22,190 --> 00:16:26,986
If we're gonna spend our lives together,

287
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:31,282
I need that spark, those butterflies,
above everything else.

288
00:16:32,242 --> 00:16:35,120
That email the other night…

289
00:16:35,203 --> 00:16:37,914
I realized my feelings didn't reach you,

290
00:16:38,081 --> 00:16:41,501
and you just never felt that spark…

291
00:16:41,751 --> 00:16:44,295
Yeah, so that was the reason.

292
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:49,259
Rather than wanting to
make you happy myself,

293
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:53,513
I just thought,
"as long as you end up happy,"

294
00:16:53,596 --> 00:16:55,432
"that's fine."

295
00:16:55,515 --> 00:16:57,183
So you're taking zero responsibility.

296
00:16:57,308 --> 00:17:00,061
That's not it.
I put myself out there over and over,

297
00:17:00,145 --> 00:17:02,230
and that was still the result.

298
00:17:03,565 --> 00:17:06,735
So I thought,
"Maybe we shouldn't see each other"

299
00:17:06,818 --> 00:17:07,944
"anymore."

300
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:10,196
So that's how you took it.

301
00:17:10,488 --> 00:17:11,865
Yeah.

302
00:17:12,991 --> 00:17:16,327
I said before I'd work in Japan,

303
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:18,830
but if I'm not with you,

304
00:17:19,247 --> 00:17:20,498
I'm…

305
00:17:21,458 --> 00:17:22,709
moving overseas.

306
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:24,794
Just because I didn't send the email,

307
00:17:24,878 --> 00:17:28,548
you jump straight to
"Guess we shouldn't be together"?

308
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:31,926
To me, it just makes your commitment
look flimsy as hell.

309
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:36,222
Calling my commitment "flimsy" is

310
00:17:36,306 --> 00:17:38,433
dead wrong.

311
00:17:38,767 --> 00:17:40,894
I thought about this over and over

312
00:17:40,977 --> 00:17:44,564
before making the call.

313
00:17:44,856 --> 00:17:46,566
Even so, I didn't receive your email.

314
00:17:46,649 --> 00:17:50,737
So I was like, "I don't get it.
What am I lacking?"

315
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:53,698
Real-world issues and "butterflies"
are different things.

316
00:17:53,948 --> 00:17:56,534
Well, that's how I interpreted it.

317
00:17:56,618 --> 00:17:59,120
I just feel like I still need

318
00:17:59,204 --> 00:18:00,789
that spark.

319
00:18:01,122 --> 00:18:03,416
Can a spark raise a child?

320
00:18:04,459 --> 00:18:07,045
Right now, Mao's the only one
actually stepping up

321
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:08,630
and taking responsibility.

322
00:18:13,551 --> 00:18:15,386
So if I had sent

323
00:18:15,470 --> 00:18:18,014
a message to you back then,

324
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:19,682
would that have remained unchanged?

325
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:22,602
Yeah, I was thinking I'd do my best.

326
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:25,605
A single message makes
that much of a difference?

327
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:28,775
I don't get that logic at all.

328
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:32,111
You keep harping on sparks,

329
00:18:32,195 --> 00:18:35,573
but I care more about
stability than sparks.

330
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:39,994
That's the only reason
I didn't message you.

331
00:18:41,246 --> 00:18:44,290
You are… and me too,

332
00:18:44,457 --> 00:18:47,544
the type to believe "love conquers all."

333
00:18:48,044 --> 00:18:49,337
Yeah.

334
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:51,631
But love couldn't pay the bills

335
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:55,760
when reality slammed into us,
and that's how it all fell apart.

336
00:19:01,558 --> 00:19:03,810
Say you go back

337
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:06,396
and start a catering job,

338
00:19:07,105 --> 00:19:09,732
making, what,

339
00:19:09,816 --> 00:19:12,569
500k yen a month?

340
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:16,114
How do you actually split that money up?

341
00:19:17,282 --> 00:19:19,951
The school fees this time

342
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:23,580
cost around 350k.

343
00:19:24,455 --> 00:19:28,334
You have to start factoring in these

344
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,503
harsh realities.

345
00:19:42,265 --> 00:19:44,392
I went to Mister Donut the other day.

346
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:48,980
I told the kids,
"Pick whatever you want for dessert."

347
00:19:49,606 --> 00:19:52,650
The younger one just grabs

348
00:19:52,734 --> 00:19:54,986
whatever he fancies,

349
00:19:55,069 --> 00:19:59,407
but the older one? He always
deliberately picks the cheaper options.

350
00:20:01,242 --> 00:20:06,247
I hate making him feel like
he has to do that.

351
00:20:07,874 --> 00:20:11,502
He's always holding back for our sake.
He's the kind of kid who says,

352
00:20:11,669 --> 00:20:13,254
"I'm fine with whatever."

353
00:20:13,963 --> 00:20:16,466
Seeing that just breaks my heart.

354
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:19,552
I tried so hard to keep things normal,

355
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:24,515
but he's constantly reading the room.

356
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:30,480
I just wanted to let him be
selfish for once.

357
00:20:37,570 --> 00:20:39,948
I just couldn't stand the instability

358
00:20:40,782 --> 00:20:42,408
anymore.

359
00:20:42,909 --> 00:20:46,621
That's why I said what I said.

360
00:20:48,831 --> 00:20:53,211
He's always been such a sweet, gentle kid.

361
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:58,174
Part of me feels like

362
00:20:59,717 --> 00:21:01,469
our drama fueled it and

363
00:21:01,552 --> 00:21:04,514
made him this way.

364
00:21:10,311 --> 00:21:12,188
I don't know what's right anymore.

365
00:21:25,368 --> 00:21:26,703
Your Highness.

366
00:21:28,538 --> 00:21:30,164
Princess Kaede.

367
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:35,086
Coming!

368
00:21:36,462 --> 00:21:38,339
I kind of wanted to chat.

369
00:21:39,674 --> 00:21:41,300
I'm heading out for lunch.

370
00:21:41,384 --> 00:21:43,052
Right now? Oh, really?

371
00:21:43,136 --> 00:21:46,889
Can we talk when I get back?

372
00:21:47,807 --> 00:21:49,767
Okay. Sorry to interrupt
while you were changing.

373
00:21:51,269 --> 00:21:54,230
You good?

374
00:22:18,796 --> 00:22:19,964
Did you get to talk?

375
00:22:20,048 --> 00:22:21,090
Yeah, we talked.

376
00:22:21,174 --> 00:22:23,259
We were wondering what's going on.

377
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:24,469
I thought he was pissed at me.

378
00:22:24,552 --> 00:22:26,387
Yeah, he was like, "Come here."

379
00:22:26,471 --> 00:22:28,264
I thought it was something serious.

380
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:31,267
I guess in his own way, it was…

381
00:22:32,685 --> 00:22:37,690
I don't know, kindness?
Trying to show he's changing.

382
00:22:38,066 --> 00:22:39,025
That's what he wanted to say?

383
00:22:39,108 --> 00:22:40,777
He was trying to show me that.

384
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:42,070
I see.

385
00:22:54,332 --> 00:22:55,666
Good morning.

386
00:22:57,752 --> 00:22:59,712
Good morning.

387
00:22:59,796 --> 00:23:01,172
Would you like to drink something?

388
00:23:01,589 --> 00:23:03,883
I'll do it myself, thanks.

389
00:23:04,258 --> 00:23:06,135
It's hot.

390
00:23:09,931 --> 00:23:11,682
Nice outfit.

391
00:23:15,103 --> 00:23:16,854
Good morning.

392
00:23:16,938 --> 00:23:18,064
So cute.

393
00:23:18,147 --> 00:23:19,107
Drink?

394
00:23:19,190 --> 00:23:21,025
Is this the one you bought?

395
00:23:21,109 --> 00:23:22,151
Yeah.

396
00:23:22,235 --> 00:23:23,194
Looks good on you.

397
00:23:23,277 --> 00:23:24,987
Might get a sunburn though.

398
00:23:25,071 --> 00:23:26,531
Where are you guys heading?

399
00:23:27,281 --> 00:23:28,699
Where are we going?

400
00:23:30,243 --> 00:23:31,994
Izakaya.

401
00:23:32,078 --> 00:23:33,329
Izakaya?

402
00:23:34,163 --> 00:23:35,706
Don't chime in at the same time!

403
00:23:37,166 --> 00:23:38,417
Kaede.

404
00:23:40,211 --> 00:23:41,420
We're off.

405
00:23:41,504 --> 00:23:42,463
Have fun!

406
00:23:43,506 --> 00:23:46,759
Total Junichi style,
rocking it like a clutch bag.

407
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:53,975
Cool.

408
00:23:56,769 --> 00:23:59,814
Looks delicious.
Totally got that Okinawa vibe.

409
00:24:00,523 --> 00:24:01,774
Let's toast.

410
00:24:02,150 --> 00:24:04,026
Here's to our final day!

411
00:24:04,110 --> 00:24:05,945
The last day.

412
00:24:06,362 --> 00:24:08,030
That went by so fast.

413
00:24:14,871 --> 00:24:16,455
Swapping drinks?

414
00:24:16,539 --> 00:24:17,957
Green flag for their chemistry.

415
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:19,709
Major move right there.

416
00:24:20,042 --> 00:24:21,752
It's good.

417
00:24:22,253 --> 00:24:23,588
I like it.

418
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:49,363
I'll finish this later.

419
00:24:50,281 --> 00:24:52,325
Pardon me.

420
00:24:52,867 --> 00:24:54,660
This is a really nice place.

421
00:24:54,744 --> 00:24:55,870
Thank you.

422
00:24:55,953 --> 00:24:56,787
My pleasure.

423
00:25:02,293 --> 00:25:03,961
There's actually something

424
00:25:04,837 --> 00:25:09,383
I want to share with you…
something I need you

425
00:25:09,467 --> 00:25:11,385
to know.

426
00:25:13,262 --> 00:25:17,558
For about seven or eight years…

427
00:25:19,393 --> 00:25:22,772
I used to work as a comedian.

428
00:25:24,315 --> 00:25:27,109
Unlocking new lore this late in the game?

429
00:25:27,193 --> 00:25:28,236
For real?

430
00:25:29,570 --> 00:25:31,656
I was in a comedy duo.

431
00:25:32,448 --> 00:25:33,658
We signed with an agency.

432
00:25:33,741 --> 00:25:35,284
Really?

433
00:25:35,701 --> 00:25:37,245
We were performing out there.

434
00:25:41,290 --> 00:25:44,794
I teamed up with
my best friend from college…

435
00:25:44,877 --> 00:25:47,672
literally my closest buddy.

436
00:25:47,755 --> 00:25:51,884
After graduating,
we both worked corporate jobs for a year.

437
00:25:51,968 --> 00:25:54,845
Then we quit

438
00:25:55,554 --> 00:26:00,309
and launched our comedy career together

439
00:26:00,393 --> 00:26:01,602
the following year.

440
00:26:03,104 --> 00:26:04,230
Amazing.

441
00:26:04,313 --> 00:26:08,109
We were based out of Fukuoka.

442
00:26:10,403 --> 00:26:12,530
Obviously, we never became

443
00:26:12,613 --> 00:26:15,283
household names,

444
00:26:15,366 --> 00:26:19,829
but we got to do TV, radio, event hosting,

445
00:26:19,912 --> 00:26:22,999
comedy gigs… all kinds of stuff

446
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:24,709
under that agency

447
00:26:25,501 --> 00:26:29,255
for about eight years.

448
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:33,259
My partner was the one
who dragged me into comedy

449
00:26:33,342 --> 00:26:35,344
in the first place.

450
00:26:35,428 --> 00:26:39,307
But then he told me
he wanted to break up the duo.

451
00:26:41,767 --> 00:26:46,897
He had a wedding, a baby on the way…
all that timing came together.

452
00:26:47,398 --> 00:26:51,402
But I was right on the verge of landing

453
00:26:51,485 --> 00:26:53,487
a regular TV gig,

454
00:26:54,155 --> 00:26:59,118
so I stayed behind
to go solo just for that show.

455
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:01,245
And…

456
00:27:06,083 --> 00:27:06,917
Oh, man…

457
00:27:08,002 --> 00:27:09,420
Are you okay?

458
00:27:11,005 --> 00:27:12,798
Part of me

459
00:27:19,972 --> 00:27:21,557
stayed solo hoping that…

460
00:27:26,354 --> 00:27:30,441
maybe he'd come back one day.

461
00:27:33,944 --> 00:27:39,742
But then Covid hit.

462
00:27:39,825 --> 00:27:42,787
With the lockdowns and
the state of emergency,

463
00:27:43,371 --> 00:27:46,665
that regular TV spot
I was so close to getting

464
00:27:46,749 --> 00:27:48,667
got completely scrapped.

465
00:27:50,836 --> 00:27:55,424
For the first time in my life,
I felt true, crushing isolation.

466
00:27:56,550 --> 00:27:58,552
I just broke inside.

467
00:28:12,274 --> 00:28:16,153
I found myself…
ready to take a step into a place

468
00:28:16,695 --> 00:28:20,366
I could never come back from.

469
00:28:27,748 --> 00:28:31,210
But then a senior comedian

470
00:28:32,086 --> 00:28:34,255
who always looked out for me

471
00:28:35,714 --> 00:28:38,259
sent me a single text.

472
00:28:40,553 --> 00:28:42,513
"You still alive?"

473
00:28:46,016 --> 00:28:50,855
That text pulled me back
from the brink just enough.

474
00:28:55,526 --> 00:29:01,115
In the end, I gave up on comedy
like a coward.

475
00:29:05,244 --> 00:29:08,164
And because of how I walked away,

476
00:29:09,540 --> 00:29:13,252
I could never see that past
as anything good.

477
00:29:14,670 --> 00:29:18,466
I've never been able to own it
or tell anyone with confidence.

478
00:29:20,551 --> 00:29:24,930
By some random stroke of luck,
I managed to scrape by

479
00:29:25,014 --> 00:29:28,309
and land a retail job in fashion.

480
00:29:29,727 --> 00:29:31,562
And one day,

481
00:29:31,937 --> 00:29:33,689
you casually asked me,

482
00:29:34,857 --> 00:29:37,485
"Do you have any big dreams"

483
00:29:37,568 --> 00:29:40,154
"or ambitions?"

484
00:29:42,698 --> 00:29:46,035
Satoshi, do you have any
big dreams or ambitions?

485
00:29:47,328 --> 00:29:48,954
Well… I do have one thing.

486
00:29:53,459 --> 00:29:55,211
I want to launch my own clothing line.

487
00:29:55,294 --> 00:29:56,128
That's nice.

488
00:29:56,212 --> 00:29:58,756
Though I'm terrified of being judged.

489
00:29:58,839 --> 00:29:59,757
Is that so?

490
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:00,925
It scares me.

491
00:30:01,258 --> 00:30:03,469
I love that you can
admit that so honestly.

492
00:30:05,971 --> 00:30:10,434
That was the first time I ever admitted

493
00:30:10,518 --> 00:30:13,604
to someone that I wanted

494
00:30:15,147 --> 00:30:16,982
my own brand.

495
00:30:17,066 --> 00:30:19,151
I finally put it into words,

496
00:30:20,402 --> 00:30:21,862
and you just gave me

497
00:30:22,404 --> 00:30:25,032
instant validation.

498
00:30:32,122 --> 00:30:36,752
In that exact moment, I had a new dream.

499
00:30:40,381 --> 00:30:45,010
I hadn't been able to
hold onto hope for so long…

500
00:30:46,303 --> 00:30:47,972
but I finally had something.

501
00:30:54,186 --> 00:30:57,606
You listened to me and
gave me that green light.

502
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:00,776
That's why

503
00:31:01,068 --> 00:31:02,987
you're so special to me, Yoko.

504
00:31:06,365 --> 00:31:07,908
Thank you.

505
00:31:09,910 --> 00:31:11,829
Thank you for telling me all of this.

506
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:18,419
It must've taken so much guts
to open up about

507
00:31:19,670 --> 00:31:21,297
what you just said.

508
00:31:23,465 --> 00:31:26,594
I'm just so glad you told me.

509
00:31:26,802 --> 00:31:27,886
Really?

510
00:31:27,970 --> 00:31:29,430
You did so well hanging in there.

511
00:31:29,513 --> 00:31:30,723
Thanks.

512
00:31:30,806 --> 00:31:33,559
Seriously… thank you for staying alive.

513
00:31:36,604 --> 00:31:38,981
I'm really glad I laid it all out there

514
00:31:39,064 --> 00:31:41,525
without holding anything back.

515
00:31:42,359 --> 00:31:45,696
Part of me didn't want to

516
00:31:46,447 --> 00:31:48,616
touch that dark past,

517
00:31:48,699 --> 00:31:51,368
but deep down, I knew Yoko was

518
00:31:51,452 --> 00:31:55,414
the one person I had to tell face-to-face.

519
00:31:55,497 --> 00:31:57,833
I had no idea how she'd react,

520
00:31:58,959 --> 00:32:02,463
but with her… I just felt like I could

521
00:32:02,546 --> 00:32:05,466
actually be vulnerable.

522
00:32:10,596 --> 00:32:11,472
What a gorgeous view.

523
00:32:11,555 --> 00:32:12,389
It's stunning.

524
00:32:12,473 --> 00:32:13,891
So nice.

525
00:32:16,185 --> 00:32:18,562
If these were a woman's legs,
it'd look pretty great.

526
00:32:18,646 --> 00:32:21,357
You know, that shot across the pool…

527
00:32:21,982 --> 00:32:23,108
Like…

528
00:32:23,192 --> 00:32:24,026
With the legs?

529
00:32:24,109 --> 00:32:25,069
Yeah.

530
00:32:26,028 --> 00:32:27,363
Like this.

531
00:32:27,446 --> 00:32:29,448
Yeah, I see it.

532
00:32:29,531 --> 00:32:32,076
I see this a lot on social media.

533
00:32:32,159 --> 00:32:33,494
Very "aesthetic".

534
00:32:35,287 --> 00:32:38,040
So did you date anyone after Hikaru?

535
00:32:38,123 --> 00:32:39,500
Nope, zero.

536
00:32:39,583 --> 00:32:40,918
Not at all.

537
00:32:41,835 --> 00:32:46,006
I didn't even have the mental bandwidth
to think about dating

538
00:32:48,676 --> 00:32:50,719
back then.

539
00:32:51,470 --> 00:32:54,932
I actually dated a girl

540
00:32:55,015 --> 00:32:57,685
who had two older kids once, too.

541
00:32:59,186 --> 00:33:00,354
Yeah.

542
00:33:00,646 --> 00:33:04,775
Even after we broke up,
she was still out there dating around.

543
00:33:04,858 --> 00:33:05,943
She was?

544
00:33:06,026 --> 00:33:07,111
Yeah, that's what I heard.

545
00:33:08,529 --> 00:33:10,072
Cool.

546
00:33:10,614 --> 00:33:13,951
I guess some people can
just pull that off.

547
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:18,163
Well, you always say life's a blast.

548
00:33:18,789 --> 00:33:20,791
So…

549
00:33:20,874 --> 00:33:25,713
Even if you take a totally new path,
I think you'll make the most of it.

550
00:33:26,296 --> 00:33:28,674
I think I can step into
a whole new chapter

551
00:33:28,757 --> 00:33:30,509
and thrive.

552
00:33:30,592 --> 00:33:35,472
I've gotta try to enjoy the ride.

553
00:33:35,556 --> 00:33:37,891
On the flip side,

554
00:33:37,975 --> 00:33:39,601
did you ever put up walls,

555
00:33:39,685 --> 00:33:41,812
telling yourself
you weren't allowed to date?

556
00:33:42,771 --> 00:33:46,608
Maybe a bit of that.
Thinking about the kids,

557
00:33:47,526 --> 00:33:50,779
or feeling like
the timing just wasn't right.

558
00:33:51,530 --> 00:33:54,992
So yeah, part of me

559
00:33:55,242 --> 00:33:59,288
thought that way.

560
00:34:01,957 --> 00:34:04,710
But kids grow up eventually.

561
00:34:04,793 --> 00:34:06,420
In three years…

562
00:34:06,503 --> 00:34:08,088
He'll be an adult, huh?

563
00:34:09,256 --> 00:34:11,759
Gosh, time flies.

564
00:34:14,386 --> 00:34:15,721
So then…

565
00:34:15,804 --> 00:34:19,641
Now that the kids are
getting up there in age,

566
00:34:20,225 --> 00:34:24,021
wouldn't it be fine to
focus on yourself a bit?

567
00:34:27,357 --> 00:34:31,320
To actually follow
your own heart for once?

568
00:34:33,989 --> 00:34:35,741
I think you should.

569
00:34:39,828 --> 00:34:43,373
Did you guys get to have
a good talk this morning?

570
00:34:45,042 --> 00:34:47,586
Yeah, we had a pretty deep talk.

571
00:34:49,463 --> 00:34:52,132
It's just, the situation itself is…

572
00:34:53,217 --> 00:34:56,804
how do I put it…
There's just so much baggage.

573
00:34:57,095 --> 00:35:00,808
And he acts completely opposite to
how he actually feels.

574
00:35:00,891 --> 00:35:02,851
He's way too contrary.

575
00:35:02,935 --> 00:35:06,480
He's probably aware of that, too.

576
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:11,068
I want to talk with him as well.

577
00:35:11,485 --> 00:35:12,444
Though I talk to him the most anyway.

578
00:35:12,528 --> 00:35:13,862
Do you?

579
00:35:14,780 --> 00:35:17,783
I mean, we look like Buddha and Jesus

580
00:35:17,866 --> 00:35:21,245
paired up together.

581
00:35:21,328 --> 00:35:22,663
That sounds like a manga.

582
00:35:22,996 --> 00:35:26,667
So I can tell the difference between his

583
00:35:26,750 --> 00:35:29,837
"I'm agonizing over something" smile
and his

584
00:35:29,920 --> 00:35:31,672
"I'm plotting something" smile.

585
00:35:32,881 --> 00:35:36,009
I might look more fragile, but…

586
00:35:36,093 --> 00:35:38,136
his heart is a microscope slide.

587
00:35:38,220 --> 00:35:40,430
Mine's made of tempered glass.

588
00:35:40,806 --> 00:35:43,016
If someone could

589
00:35:43,100 --> 00:35:45,143
just sit right in the middle of

590
00:35:45,227 --> 00:35:47,354
those polar opposites,

591
00:35:47,938 --> 00:35:49,815
that'd probably be the sweet spot.

592
00:35:49,898 --> 00:35:51,233
Right.

593
00:35:51,316 --> 00:35:53,986
I got so much inspiration from him.

594
00:35:54,069 --> 00:35:55,654
Really?

595
00:35:55,988 --> 00:35:58,699
He keeps saying he wants to change, too.

596
00:36:03,036 --> 00:36:06,874
So yeah, I think it was good that
you invited him here.

597
00:36:09,126 --> 00:36:12,212
I'd like to think so.

598
00:36:17,509 --> 00:36:19,761
I'm glad she's having fun.

599
00:36:19,845 --> 00:36:24,433
She needed a break
to forget about real life for a bit.

600
00:36:28,770 --> 00:36:30,606
Hikaru.

601
00:36:30,689 --> 00:36:31,857
Hikaru.

602
00:36:40,991 --> 00:36:42,701
What's he looking at?

603
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:56,298
Kids are everything, and they're innocent.

604
00:36:56,381 --> 00:37:00,385
It's about how you step up
to protect them.

605
00:37:00,928 --> 00:37:02,304
Even today,

606
00:37:02,387 --> 00:37:05,641
Mao was the one
who gave me yet another last chance.

607
00:37:06,433 --> 00:37:09,186
I realized I hadn't changed one bit.

608
00:37:10,354 --> 00:37:12,648
I feel so terrible about that.

609
00:37:12,731 --> 00:37:15,484
I really, deeply feel like
I owe her an apology.

610
00:37:16,151 --> 00:37:19,738
If she actually lets me stay
in her life after this…

611
00:37:20,072 --> 00:37:21,990
I need to get my act together.

612
00:37:24,368 --> 00:37:26,745
I have to be more honest with myself…

613
00:37:27,913 --> 00:37:30,332
…and consider Mao's feelings

614
00:37:30,749 --> 00:37:34,252
and be there for her.

615
00:37:36,630 --> 00:37:38,423
I think that's…

616
00:37:40,717 --> 00:37:43,053
the main thing

617
00:37:43,887 --> 00:37:48,433
I have to work on from here on out.

618
00:38:06,118 --> 00:38:09,079
Alright, so Hikaru's had
a total shift in mindset.

619
00:38:09,162 --> 00:38:10,831
He was being petty and sulking before,

620
00:38:10,914 --> 00:38:15,210
but hearing that donut shop story
about his kids finally snapped him

621
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:16,378
back to reality.

622
00:38:16,461 --> 00:38:21,425
That donut story is probably just
the tip of the iceberg.

623
00:38:21,508 --> 00:38:23,552
There are so many
other struggles like that.

624
00:38:24,761 --> 00:38:26,680
There are probably

625
00:38:26,763 --> 00:38:30,517
13 stories just like that donut one
happening every single day.

626
00:38:30,851 --> 00:38:32,227
Just the tip of the iceberg.

627
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:36,106
Mao probably didn't want to
weigh him down with all of it,

628
00:38:36,189 --> 00:38:39,401
so she kept quiet about most of it.

629
00:38:39,484 --> 00:38:41,445
So when he completely glossed over

630
00:38:41,528 --> 00:38:43,071
those real-world struggles,

631
00:38:43,155 --> 00:38:46,658
and wrote her off just because
there were no sparks,

632
00:38:46,742 --> 00:38:49,911
not to mention
straight-up ignoring her to her face,

633
00:38:50,078 --> 00:38:53,874
saying all sorts of things…

634
00:38:53,957 --> 00:38:55,584
that must've been

635
00:38:55,667 --> 00:38:59,212
a total gut punch for Mao at the time.

636
00:38:59,296 --> 00:39:02,716
And considering everything Mao's carrying,

637
00:39:02,799 --> 00:39:06,595
Ryo is definitely giving her

638
00:39:06,678 --> 00:39:09,514
a totally different kind of energy.

639
00:39:09,598 --> 00:39:11,892
You could totally see it in her

640
00:39:11,975 --> 00:39:14,227
smile and her reactions,

641
00:39:14,311 --> 00:39:17,022
so I really want her to

642
00:39:17,105 --> 00:39:19,816
start putting herself first for once.

643
00:39:21,777 --> 00:39:23,278
Where should we go? Shall we get a tan?

644
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:24,196
Sure.

645
00:39:24,279 --> 00:39:25,864
Let's do that, then.

646
00:39:25,947 --> 00:39:27,199
Let's go.

647
00:39:29,576 --> 00:39:31,161
So how are things?

648
00:39:32,162 --> 00:39:36,124
I mean, what he was telling me
a few hours ago

649
00:39:36,208 --> 00:39:40,337
is completely different. He kept insisting

650
00:39:41,421 --> 00:39:44,508
he was totally devoted to me, so honestly,

651
00:39:44,591 --> 00:39:47,511
I was really torn, like…

652
00:39:47,594 --> 00:39:49,429
what should I do?

653
00:39:49,513 --> 00:39:53,433
I need to find an answer to that.

654
00:39:53,517 --> 00:39:56,353
If we left this place together,
I knew I had to be

655
00:39:56,436 --> 00:39:58,688
100% committed to that decision.

656
00:39:58,772 --> 00:40:00,941
And then yesterday,

657
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:04,778
he didn't say a single word to me
and spent the whole time talking to Kaede.

658
00:40:07,364 --> 00:40:08,740
Like…

659
00:40:11,576 --> 00:40:12,869
This hurts so much.

660
00:40:12,953 --> 00:40:16,790
This is exactly why
I stayed away from romance,

661
00:40:16,873 --> 00:40:19,793
because deep down
I knew it would end like this.

662
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:22,337
I knew it'd always end up like this.

663
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:24,339
That's why I'm on my own right now.

664
00:40:24,881 --> 00:40:27,759
If my marriage had actually worked out,

665
00:40:27,843 --> 00:40:30,220
I wouldn't even be here.

666
00:40:33,682 --> 00:40:36,017
Wish we had another day or two.

667
00:40:36,101 --> 00:40:37,310
Yeah.

668
00:40:39,187 --> 00:40:43,358
I'm in a totally different mindset now
compared to when I first arrived.

669
00:40:43,441 --> 00:40:45,026
It's crazy.

670
00:40:48,029 --> 00:40:50,907
Did you picture yourself like this
before you got here?

671
00:40:50,991 --> 00:40:54,327
Not at all.
It turned out completely different.

672
00:40:55,328 --> 00:40:57,914
I thought we'd at least have

673
00:40:57,998 --> 00:41:01,251
more opportunities for one-on-one chats

674
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:03,753
but we barely had any.

675
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:05,797
That's why I said "painful".

676
00:41:09,926 --> 00:41:11,970
Did I tell you? I asked Yoko

677
00:41:12,053 --> 00:41:13,805
if she wanted to get in
the jacuzzi with me,

678
00:41:14,890 --> 00:41:16,474
but she didn't want to.

679
00:41:16,558 --> 00:41:17,809
Really?

680
00:41:18,226 --> 00:41:20,854
On past dates, I was

681
00:41:20,937 --> 00:41:22,689
always the only one jumping in

682
00:41:23,315 --> 00:41:24,566
while she just sat on the sidelines.

683
00:41:24,649 --> 00:41:25,483
I see.

684
00:41:25,567 --> 00:41:26,693
Yeah.

685
00:41:27,277 --> 00:41:30,071
So when you actually

686
00:41:30,155 --> 00:41:32,741
jumped in the pool and jacuzzi with me

687
00:41:32,866 --> 00:41:34,618
and we talked a lot…

688
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:37,537
I was like, "This is what I wanted."

689
00:41:38,663 --> 00:41:40,624
He suddenly got a taste of the fun part.

690
00:41:40,707 --> 00:41:42,584
He must've had a blast.

691
00:41:43,627 --> 00:41:47,297
If he moved on from me, that's fine.

692
00:41:47,422 --> 00:41:48,924
Honestly,

693
00:41:49,007 --> 00:41:51,384
I'd genuinely want to
cheer him on as a friend.

694
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:53,470
But…

695
00:41:53,553 --> 00:41:56,264
if that's the case,
I wish he'd say it to my face.

696
00:41:59,351 --> 00:42:02,812
Bottom line, that's the exact kind
of thing about him that

697
00:42:02,896 --> 00:42:04,022
turned me off.

698
00:42:04,648 --> 00:42:07,525
Until now, we stayed friends
because he's a good,

699
00:42:07,609 --> 00:42:09,903
sincere, devoted guy,

700
00:42:09,986 --> 00:42:12,530
and having that attention felt good.

701
00:42:12,614 --> 00:42:13,949
It's selfish of me, sure,

702
00:42:15,408 --> 00:42:17,577
but I don't have a boyfriend.

703
00:42:20,497 --> 00:42:22,707
So yeah, maybe I am being selfish.

704
00:42:22,832 --> 00:42:25,877
He might say, "Well, you had time

705
00:42:25,961 --> 00:42:28,421
yesterday and the day before too."

706
00:42:28,505 --> 00:42:29,756
But…

707
00:42:32,384 --> 00:42:34,552
Still, it all comes down to timing, right?

708
00:42:34,636 --> 00:42:37,806
Exactly. It's only hitting me now.

709
00:42:46,898 --> 00:42:48,817
I was so blinded by the idea of love

710
00:42:48,900 --> 00:42:50,527
that I couldn't see the reality.

711
00:42:51,820 --> 00:42:53,738
What does loving someone even mean?

712
00:42:54,781 --> 00:42:55,949
Love…

713
00:43:00,203 --> 00:43:02,330
Hold on, let me eat Goya Champuru.

714
00:43:03,665 --> 00:43:05,166
That's funny. I like it.

715
00:43:05,667 --> 00:43:07,627
I get you'd want to eat Goya Champuru.

716
00:43:12,882 --> 00:43:14,634
Isn't it just about
wanting to be with them?

717
00:43:15,802 --> 00:43:17,304
I agree.

718
00:43:17,429 --> 00:43:19,931
Can you picture it? With me?

719
00:43:20,015 --> 00:43:20,890
Yeah.

720
00:43:22,225 --> 00:43:24,185
"With me", she said.

721
00:43:25,687 --> 00:43:27,480
What do you think of my answer, Sensei?

722
00:43:29,733 --> 00:43:32,485
I've been trying to solve all these
emotional riddles,

723
00:43:33,278 --> 00:43:34,863
and missing the mark almost every time.

724
00:43:36,740 --> 00:43:38,033
I don't think you missed.

725
00:43:38,116 --> 00:43:40,994
If that's what you genuinely feel.

726
00:43:41,369 --> 00:43:43,538
Yeah, she just said it was wrong.

727
00:43:43,621 --> 00:43:45,332
In my head it was right,

728
00:43:45,999 --> 00:43:47,250
but who knows.

729
00:43:50,837 --> 00:43:54,090
But deep down,
Yoko's still at your core, isn't she?

730
00:43:54,716 --> 00:43:56,509
Of course she is.

731
00:43:56,718 --> 00:43:59,512
Like today, it's obvious to her that

732
00:43:59,763 --> 00:44:03,058
I'm approaching you.

733
00:44:03,850 --> 00:44:06,186
She probably thinks I'm the worst.

734
00:44:06,728 --> 00:44:08,313
You think so?

735
00:44:08,396 --> 00:44:10,398
Yeah, probably.

736
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:24,579
She's probably dealing with a lot of

737
00:44:24,662 --> 00:44:27,999
her own baggage too right now.

738
00:44:28,958 --> 00:44:32,921
Kaede's conversational rhythm is top-tier.

739
00:44:33,004 --> 00:44:36,049
Playful one second, locking eyes the next…

740
00:44:36,132 --> 00:44:37,967
She's really good at this.

741
00:44:38,259 --> 00:44:39,302
I'm okay.

742
00:44:39,886 --> 00:44:42,347
Thanks for hearing me out.

743
00:44:42,430 --> 00:44:44,474
Wait, what is this?

744
00:44:45,517 --> 00:44:47,727
A team-building exercise.

745
00:44:51,481 --> 00:44:53,191
Oh, do you mind?

746
00:44:56,319 --> 00:44:57,779
We're back.

747
00:44:57,862 --> 00:44:59,531
We're back.

748
00:44:59,614 --> 00:45:00,448
Did you go for a swim?

749
00:45:00,532 --> 00:45:01,533
Not yet.

750
00:45:01,616 --> 00:45:02,492
No?

751
00:45:02,867 --> 00:45:04,160
Thinking about taking a dip now.

752
00:45:04,244 --> 00:45:05,078
Why not?

753
00:45:05,161 --> 00:45:05,995
Let's go.

754
00:45:06,496 --> 00:45:07,330
Yoko, coming?

755
00:45:07,414 --> 00:45:08,248
Pass.

756
00:45:08,331 --> 00:45:09,165
No?

757
00:45:09,249 --> 00:45:10,959
We were talking over there earlier,

758
00:45:11,042 --> 00:45:12,794
but the sun got harsh so I moved here.

759
00:45:12,877 --> 00:45:14,212
I see.

760
00:45:14,337 --> 00:45:15,922
Alright, pool time.

761
00:45:16,840 --> 00:45:19,175
Why are there weird ripples over there?

762
00:45:19,592 --> 00:45:21,010
In the middle.

763
00:45:22,679 --> 00:45:24,514
Daichi's not going either?

764
00:45:24,597 --> 00:45:27,475
Must be awkward
leaving her sitting there all alone.

765
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:28,435
Ah, right.

766
00:45:28,518 --> 00:45:29,853
Leaving her alone…

767
00:45:29,936 --> 00:45:31,604
My bad, you're right.

768
00:45:31,688 --> 00:45:33,731
So pretty.

769
00:45:34,274 --> 00:45:35,442
New swimsuit?

770
00:45:35,775 --> 00:45:38,862
Daichi's keeping quiet,

771
00:45:38,987 --> 00:45:40,780
but he's definitely worried about her.

772
00:45:40,864 --> 00:45:42,532
Can you swim?

773
00:45:42,615 --> 00:45:44,033
I can.

774
00:45:44,117 --> 00:45:45,410
Really?

775
00:45:46,661 --> 00:45:47,829
They're swimming together.

776
00:45:47,912 --> 00:45:49,205
Go on, enjoy it.

777
00:45:49,831 --> 00:45:51,249
Live it up.

778
00:45:53,751 --> 00:45:56,171
I swear I've got 20/10 vision right now.

779
00:45:57,589 --> 00:45:59,215
Get in there, Hiroyoshi!

780
00:46:07,891 --> 00:46:09,476
Final day.

781
00:46:14,147 --> 00:46:16,149
But this isn't jealousy, right?

782
00:46:16,232 --> 00:46:19,068
No, it's not.

783
00:46:19,611 --> 00:46:21,279
I think you do still have a bit.

784
00:46:21,529 --> 00:46:22,572
What?

785
00:46:22,655 --> 00:46:24,073
Just a little bit.

786
00:46:24,324 --> 00:46:26,201
Otherwise, it wouldn't bother you so much.

787
00:46:28,161 --> 00:46:30,455
He's totally talking about himself now.

788
00:46:30,580 --> 00:46:32,999
Yeah. They're basically doing
mutual therapy.

789
00:46:33,082 --> 00:46:34,709
Comforting each other.

790
00:46:39,130 --> 00:46:40,632
Not gonna talk about your previous job?

791
00:46:41,633 --> 00:46:42,759
I haven't told anyone.

792
00:46:42,842 --> 00:46:44,219
That's a super specific callback.

793
00:46:44,302 --> 00:46:47,055
So Kanako knows he used to be a comedian.

794
00:46:47,138 --> 00:46:50,642
But I finally told Yoko earlier.

795
00:46:50,725 --> 00:46:52,018
You did?

796
00:46:53,228 --> 00:46:54,771
I wanted to say it so many times.

797
00:46:54,854 --> 00:46:57,065
I came so close to blurting it out

798
00:46:57,148 --> 00:46:58,316
when I was mad,

799
00:46:58,399 --> 00:47:00,401
but I knew you'd hate it.

800
00:47:00,485 --> 00:47:03,071
Thanks. Seriously, thank you.

801
00:47:04,864 --> 00:47:07,367
I was just dragging my feet.

802
00:47:07,450 --> 00:47:10,119
I kept thinking

803
00:47:10,203 --> 00:47:12,872
I should bring it up with just the guys,
but I couldn't.

804
00:47:14,207 --> 00:47:18,002
Still, I made sure Yoko heard it
directly from me.

805
00:47:21,548 --> 00:47:23,508
I see.

806
00:47:26,511 --> 00:47:29,681
Hey, does this smell like a dusty closet?

807
00:47:29,889 --> 00:47:31,057
Am I good?

808
00:47:31,140 --> 00:47:31,975
Stop.

809
00:47:32,350 --> 00:47:34,102
Please, can you check?

810
00:47:34,185 --> 00:47:35,186
No.

811
00:47:35,520 --> 00:47:36,896
I don't know… it smells.

812
00:47:37,021 --> 00:47:38,481
It does?

813
00:47:38,815 --> 00:47:40,650
I'm screwed then.

814
00:47:41,150 --> 00:47:42,944
Kanako's laughing.

815
00:47:43,194 --> 00:47:44,612
I don't even know anymore.

816
00:47:44,696 --> 00:47:46,698
I had this packed in a box forever.

817
00:47:47,699 --> 00:47:50,493
Wanted to see if it smelled bad,

818
00:47:50,577 --> 00:47:53,538
so I asked, and she said it smells.

819
00:47:54,539 --> 00:47:56,708
Your whole persona
just completely flipped.

820
00:47:56,791 --> 00:47:57,959
I haven't changed.

821
00:47:58,042 --> 00:47:59,043
You have.

822
00:47:59,127 --> 00:48:01,254
This is the side of you I wanted to see.

823
00:48:01,546 --> 00:48:04,465
What was with that
fake front this whole time?

824
00:48:04,549 --> 00:48:06,050
I was like, "Who the hell are you?"

825
00:48:07,385 --> 00:48:08,386
You're totally different.

826
00:48:08,469 --> 00:48:09,971
Why do we find out on the final day?

827
00:48:10,054 --> 00:48:11,723
Right? Way too late.

828
00:48:11,806 --> 00:48:13,099
Go pour me another one.

829
00:48:15,893 --> 00:48:17,854
That's funny, I like it.

830
00:48:17,937 --> 00:48:19,897
This guy is absolute chaos.

831
00:48:22,817 --> 00:48:24,193
Wonder if any sea grapes
washed up around here.

832
00:48:24,277 --> 00:48:25,111
You ate some today.

833
00:48:25,194 --> 00:48:26,112
I did.

834
00:48:26,195 --> 00:48:27,739
Was it good?

835
00:48:27,822 --> 00:48:28,906
It was really good.

836
00:48:28,990 --> 00:48:30,283
Look at them…

837
00:48:30,366 --> 00:48:31,743
finally getting their alone time.

838
00:48:33,494 --> 00:48:34,537
Is this a hermit crab?

839
00:48:34,621 --> 00:48:35,580
Yeah.

840
00:48:37,206 --> 00:48:39,334
Oh, cute.

841
00:48:44,464 --> 00:48:45,673
I'll hold it.

842
00:48:45,757 --> 00:48:46,758
I'm alright.

843
00:48:48,718 --> 00:48:49,802
Don't fall.

844
00:48:49,886 --> 00:48:52,597
Me? Yeah, could happen.

845
00:48:54,974 --> 00:48:57,185
Great shot by the camera crew just now.

846
00:48:57,310 --> 00:48:58,603
Nice.

847
00:48:58,686 --> 00:49:00,647
So symbolic.

848
00:49:02,565 --> 00:49:05,234
By the way, why did you ask me
if I was okay today?

849
00:49:05,985 --> 00:49:08,029
Because you looked anxious.

850
00:49:08,863 --> 00:49:10,323
Wow, you saw it.

851
00:49:14,494 --> 00:49:16,454
I mean, like I wrote in the letter…

852
00:49:16,537 --> 00:49:20,458
I went through a really dark period.
My friends walked away,

853
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:23,294
my family drifted apart… and I think,

854
00:49:23,378 --> 00:49:25,463
that's where all of this comes from.

855
00:49:25,880 --> 00:49:29,384
I just can't stand the thought of
people leaving me anymore.

856
00:49:30,635 --> 00:49:33,513
So instead of making a real move,

857
00:49:34,806 --> 00:49:39,477
I chose the safe path, keeping you
at arm's length

858
00:49:39,560 --> 00:49:41,521
so I'd never lose you.

859
00:49:42,689 --> 00:49:45,942
So when we became friends,

860
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:49,612
it was because we thought,

861
00:49:49,696 --> 00:49:53,199
"Friendship is the one thing
that never has to end."

862
00:49:53,282 --> 00:49:55,827
You chose that route

863
00:49:58,454 --> 00:50:00,957
because with friends,

864
00:50:01,040 --> 00:50:03,376
walking away isn't an option.

865
00:50:03,459 --> 00:50:05,920
So are you saying
you're fine settling for that?

866
00:50:06,003 --> 00:50:09,048
No, that's not it.

867
00:50:11,509 --> 00:50:13,344
That's not enough.

868
00:50:15,179 --> 00:50:17,390
I don't want that safety net.

869
00:50:18,474 --> 00:50:20,685
That's why I brought up the whole
"all or nothing" thing.

870
00:50:23,146 --> 00:50:24,897
Right now,

871
00:50:25,356 --> 00:50:28,735
I simply want to be with you.

872
00:50:28,901 --> 00:50:30,820
Whether we actually want to be
together or not…

873
00:50:30,903 --> 00:50:31,904
Right.

874
00:50:33,489 --> 00:50:37,452
Either we stay together,
or we never see each other again.

875
00:50:37,535 --> 00:50:39,537
Isn't that super extreme?

876
00:50:39,620 --> 00:50:42,123
Isn't that what it comes down to?

877
00:50:48,296 --> 00:50:50,840
I don't know,
but isn't that a real possibility?

878
00:50:55,553 --> 00:50:58,473
So if you had to pick, which is it?

879
00:50:59,474 --> 00:51:00,975
That's way too extreme.

880
00:51:01,058 --> 00:51:02,143
It is.

881
00:51:06,981 --> 00:51:08,357
Practically an ultimatum.

882
00:51:10,193 --> 00:51:11,736
Totally extreme.

883
00:51:11,819 --> 00:51:13,196
Straight-up blackmail.

884
00:51:22,079 --> 00:51:24,165
My answer is clear…

885
00:51:25,833 --> 00:51:29,879
going back to being friends
is off the table.

886
00:51:32,840 --> 00:51:35,593
We're staying together forever.

887
00:51:36,594 --> 00:51:40,765
That's my call.

888
00:51:47,939 --> 00:51:51,609
I mean, you know I'm not looking for

889
00:51:51,692 --> 00:51:54,779
some flashy, high-glam lifestyle, right?

890
00:51:54,862 --> 00:51:56,072
I know.

891
00:51:56,489 --> 00:51:58,908
All I really want is

892
00:51:59,867 --> 00:52:04,163
to feel that spark again.

893
00:52:05,039 --> 00:52:07,041
Honestly, when…

894
00:52:07,291 --> 00:52:10,378
two people who broke up
give it another shot,

895
00:52:10,461 --> 00:52:13,923
isn't that the only thing that matters?

896
00:52:14,549 --> 00:52:15,424
Is that how you feel?

897
00:52:15,508 --> 00:52:16,384
Yeah.

898
00:52:16,717 --> 00:52:19,095
I can't think of anything else.

899
00:52:19,178 --> 00:52:22,306
It's not like I have dealbreakers with you
or dislike anything about you.

900
00:52:23,099 --> 00:52:26,060
What I need most in love is excitement.

901
00:52:26,894 --> 00:52:30,314
Not like teenage butterflies, but still.

902
00:52:30,398 --> 00:52:31,607
But still?

903
00:52:31,691 --> 00:52:33,067
But…

904
00:52:33,150 --> 00:52:35,862
You've just been playing
the safe, protective

905
00:52:37,071 --> 00:52:38,531
big brother…

906
00:52:38,614 --> 00:52:39,907
This whole time.

907
00:52:39,991 --> 00:52:40,950
Protecting who?

908
00:52:41,033 --> 00:52:43,744
Me. Always so cool and composed.

909
00:52:43,828 --> 00:52:45,454
Wait, I'm acting like a big brother?

910
00:52:45,538 --> 00:52:46,873
That's how it felt.

911
00:52:46,956 --> 00:52:49,375
Like, "She'll come back to me eventually."

912
00:52:49,458 --> 00:52:51,210
I did say something like that
the other day.

913
00:52:51,294 --> 00:52:54,755
So she's definitely still feeling
that lack of excitement.

914
00:52:54,839 --> 00:52:57,383
She knows he's just gonna go along with

915
00:52:57,466 --> 00:52:58,885
whatever she says.

916
00:52:58,968 --> 00:53:02,555
He never gets angry or
genuinely worked up.

917
00:53:02,638 --> 00:53:04,891
I see. So that's part of the issue too.

918
00:53:05,516 --> 00:53:08,352
I intentionally invited you over
to my place before, right?

919
00:53:08,436 --> 00:53:09,729
You did.

920
00:53:12,773 --> 00:53:15,026
We got yakitori takeout.

921
00:53:15,109 --> 00:53:16,319
We did.

922
00:53:16,402 --> 00:53:17,862
I invited you to the festival, too.

923
00:53:17,945 --> 00:53:19,155
You did.

924
00:53:19,780 --> 00:53:22,617
You gave me so many chances.

925
00:53:23,159 --> 00:53:24,827
I know.

926
00:53:26,120 --> 00:53:27,997
I get it.

927
00:53:30,249 --> 00:53:32,418
But back then,

928
00:53:32,501 --> 00:53:35,046
I thought keeping total boundaries
was the right move.

929
00:53:35,838 --> 00:53:37,715
So…

930
00:53:38,424 --> 00:53:41,260
if I made you feel hurt

931
00:53:41,344 --> 00:53:43,930
back then… then I'm sorry.

932
00:53:45,890 --> 00:53:48,351
You really are attractive.

933
00:53:48,726 --> 00:53:50,311
That stings right now.

934
00:53:51,062 --> 00:53:52,939
Hearing that hurts even more.

935
00:53:53,022 --> 00:53:54,523
Because you made me say it?

936
00:53:54,607 --> 00:53:56,233
No, you didn't force anything.

937
00:53:58,402 --> 00:54:01,197
Ever since my divorce,

938
00:54:01,280 --> 00:54:05,534
I completely gave up on improving myself

939
00:54:05,618 --> 00:54:08,579
or ever being seen as a man again.

940
00:54:08,996 --> 00:54:12,541
I couldn't even picture
sharing a life with someone.

941
00:54:13,292 --> 00:54:16,253
I basically checked out.

942
00:54:17,129 --> 00:54:22,426
But everything Kaede's given me…

943
00:54:23,594 --> 00:54:27,848
feels like a push to

944
00:54:27,932 --> 00:54:30,851
finally move forward.

945
00:54:32,019 --> 00:54:36,524
I used to operate on
an all-or-nothing mindset,

946
00:54:36,649 --> 00:54:41,570
but to keep this at 100%,
I have to step up

947
00:54:42,488 --> 00:54:44,824
and become the kind of man

948
00:54:45,533 --> 00:54:47,326
who makes her heart race.

949
00:54:49,412 --> 00:54:51,455
So this time,

950
00:54:51,789 --> 00:54:54,959
I'm going to be the one
giving you constant green lights.

951
00:55:01,716 --> 00:55:04,301
Guess that's his nature.
He's super low-key.

952
00:55:07,138 --> 00:55:11,100
A lot's gone down, huh?
In such a short time.

953
00:55:11,183 --> 00:55:13,894
Yeah.

954
00:55:13,978 --> 00:55:15,396
A whole lot.

955
00:55:16,063 --> 00:55:17,940
Hey… can I get just five minutes with you?

956
00:55:18,024 --> 00:55:19,859
Right now? Oh, sure.

957
00:55:20,401 --> 00:55:22,445
We'll be back in five minutes.

958
00:55:22,528 --> 00:55:23,863
Five minutes? That's it?

959
00:55:23,946 --> 00:55:25,322
Just five minutes?

960
00:55:25,865 --> 00:55:28,034
They're black and white.

961
00:55:29,869 --> 00:55:31,579
Intense.

962
00:55:33,622 --> 00:55:36,208
It's not that cold today.

963
00:55:36,542 --> 00:55:38,210
Yeah, this weather is pretty nice.

964
00:55:39,503 --> 00:55:40,838
Mind if I go first?

965
00:55:40,921 --> 00:55:42,173
Go ahead.

966
00:55:45,092 --> 00:55:48,012
Something really hit me today.

967
00:55:48,095 --> 00:55:53,809
I spent all this time
holding grudges against you,

968
00:55:53,893 --> 00:55:56,228
feeling like we were on

969
00:55:56,312 --> 00:55:59,690
completely different wavelengths.

970
00:56:01,442 --> 00:56:04,028
But it was never your problem.

971
00:56:04,111 --> 00:56:06,947
You didn't do anything wrong.
You have your

972
00:56:07,031 --> 00:56:10,451
own good qualities.

973
00:56:10,534 --> 00:56:13,454
I was just being petty.

974
00:56:13,537 --> 00:56:16,248
I kept getting so worked up,

975
00:56:17,750 --> 00:56:21,295
but that's on me.
I need to do some growing up.

976
00:56:21,796 --> 00:56:23,422
So… I'm sorry.

977
00:56:23,506 --> 00:56:24,924
I'm sorry for everything.

978
00:56:25,007 --> 00:56:26,217
Don't worry about it.

979
00:56:27,968 --> 00:56:30,012
I kept replaying what you

980
00:56:30,096 --> 00:56:33,349
always ask me, "Why me?"

981
00:56:33,682 --> 00:56:36,560
"Why do you even like me?"

982
00:56:37,103 --> 00:56:39,688
And I realized…

983
00:56:39,897 --> 00:56:41,148
I was just

984
00:56:41,232 --> 00:56:44,652
chasing the ghost of who you used to be.

985
00:56:44,985 --> 00:56:48,072
That's why you kept asking, "Why me?"

986
00:56:48,155 --> 00:56:51,033
Because I wasn't even looking at
who you really are.

987
00:56:51,367 --> 00:56:55,037
I was obsessed with bringing back
that brief moment when you were

988
00:56:55,121 --> 00:56:56,747
head over heels for me,

989
00:56:56,831 --> 00:57:00,084
looking at me with those shining eyes.

990
00:57:00,417 --> 00:57:03,212
I kept believing
if I just tried hard enough,

991
00:57:03,295 --> 00:57:05,131
I could get that back.

992
00:57:05,631 --> 00:57:07,258
But this time…

993
00:57:07,341 --> 00:57:11,595
I finally felt it deep down.
I'm just not the guy for you.

994
00:57:13,722 --> 00:57:17,101
And then the next day Kaede goes,

995
00:57:17,184 --> 00:57:19,311
"We're here anyway,
let's hit the jacuzzi."

996
00:57:19,395 --> 00:57:21,522
Truth is, we never got to

997
00:57:22,648 --> 00:57:26,026
just hang out as a couple.

998
00:57:27,194 --> 00:57:29,989
I know there were things
you didn't feel like doing,

999
00:57:30,072 --> 00:57:33,117
but I realized that's what I
actually wanted out of a date.

1000
00:57:33,784 --> 00:57:37,121
When Kaede just casually invited me…

1001
00:57:37,204 --> 00:57:39,582
I couldn't help but find that
really sweet.

1002
00:57:40,958 --> 00:57:43,627
But up until now,

1003
00:57:44,879 --> 00:57:46,589
you know…

1004
00:57:48,465 --> 00:57:52,011
you were my whole drive.

1005
00:57:52,094 --> 00:57:55,764
You were my whole reason to keep pushing.

1006
00:57:56,307 --> 00:57:58,517
Everything I've made it through…

1007
00:58:00,561 --> 00:58:02,438
is all thanks to you.

1008
00:58:05,065 --> 00:58:07,818
I wanted to be that man for you,

1009
00:58:08,444 --> 00:58:10,779
but maybe it just wasn't meant to be.

1010
00:58:12,865 --> 00:58:17,119
All I ever wanted was

1011
00:58:17,203 --> 00:58:22,625
to pour everything I had

1012
00:58:25,085 --> 00:58:28,255
into making you happy.

1013
00:58:28,964 --> 00:58:30,549
So…

1014
00:58:31,467 --> 00:58:32,635
if that made you happy,

1015
00:58:32,718 --> 00:58:33,969
even just a little bit…

1016
00:58:34,053 --> 00:58:36,889
then you did give back.

1017
00:58:36,972 --> 00:58:39,266
You said you gave me nothing,

1018
00:58:40,267 --> 00:58:42,311
but you gave me everything.

1019
00:58:42,728 --> 00:58:45,147
You're making me cry.

1020
00:58:46,607 --> 00:58:47,816
I…

1021
00:58:47,900 --> 00:58:50,653
I never expected payback.

1022
00:58:51,111 --> 00:58:54,156
Just seeing that smile

1023
00:58:55,407 --> 00:58:58,160
and the words,

1024
00:58:58,244 --> 00:59:02,248
"thank you" was enough for me.

1025
00:59:05,292 --> 00:59:09,213
You gave me so much strength,

1026
00:59:09,296 --> 00:59:11,006
Yoko.

1027
00:59:11,674 --> 00:59:15,594
Wanting us to keep lifting each other up

1028
00:59:16,303 --> 00:59:18,806
and being the man who supports you…

1029
00:59:18,889 --> 00:59:22,893
none of that was ever a lie.

1030
00:59:25,938 --> 00:59:28,315
Wait… I'm getting teary.

1031
00:59:30,025 --> 00:59:32,778
We had amazing times,

1032
00:59:32,861 --> 00:59:35,698
and yeah, some really painful ones too.

1033
00:59:35,781 --> 00:59:37,658
Yesterday, you summed it all up right?

1034
00:59:37,741 --> 00:59:38,575
Summed it up?

1035
00:59:38,993 --> 00:59:41,620
When they asked for one word,
you said "painful".

1036
00:59:41,704 --> 00:59:44,665
I felt so bad and

1037
00:59:44,748 --> 00:59:46,625
wanted to apologize, but…

1038
00:59:46,709 --> 00:59:48,836
I just didn't have the capacity to do so.

1039
00:59:48,919 --> 00:59:50,629
Don't even worry about it.

1040
00:59:52,673 --> 00:59:56,593
Today made me realize

1041
00:59:56,677 --> 00:59:58,721
why I kept avoiding

1042
00:59:58,804 --> 01:00:01,598
relationships for so long.

1043
01:00:01,682 --> 01:00:04,018
Even a guy who spent years

1044
01:00:04,101 --> 01:00:08,439
completely devoted to me
can fall out of love.

1045
01:00:08,689 --> 01:00:11,775
Stuff like this terrified me so much

1046
01:00:11,859 --> 01:00:13,736
that I just avoided love altogether.

1047
01:00:15,279 --> 01:00:20,034
I mean, nobody's gonna chase you forever.

1048
01:00:21,577 --> 01:00:24,413
But I know that's my own issue.

1049
01:00:26,498 --> 01:00:28,834
I've always had that trauma…

1050
01:00:34,256 --> 01:00:36,133
You know…

1051
01:00:38,177 --> 01:00:41,805
When I put my heart out there

1052
01:00:41,889 --> 01:00:44,058
and got nothing back,

1053
01:00:44,141 --> 01:00:47,061
I just figured,
"I'm not the right guy for her."

1054
01:00:47,478 --> 01:00:50,939
So next time you fall for someone…

1055
01:00:51,815 --> 01:00:54,026
don't hold back.

1056
01:00:55,277 --> 01:00:58,238
Just give that love right back.

1057
01:00:58,947 --> 01:01:03,369
That was just me being immature.

1058
01:01:10,626 --> 01:01:12,795
Thank you for everything.

1059
01:01:12,878 --> 01:01:15,297
A million thank you's
and a million sorry's.

1060
01:01:15,381 --> 01:01:16,840
Same here.

1061
01:01:30,896 --> 01:01:33,982
And now, moving on to Yoko and Hiroyoshi…

1062
01:01:34,066 --> 01:01:36,193
You did great, Hiroyoshi.

1063
01:01:36,276 --> 01:01:40,489
Honestly, seeing Yoko realize

1064
01:01:40,572 --> 01:01:43,826
where she went wrong

1065
01:01:43,909 --> 01:01:46,745
and actually apologize for it…

1066
01:01:46,995 --> 01:01:48,831
that really touched me.

1067
01:01:48,914 --> 01:01:51,542
They finally had a real,
honest conversation.

1068
01:01:52,292 --> 01:01:55,504
Maybe for the first time
on this whole trip.

1069
01:01:55,587 --> 01:01:59,174
Now, as for Kaede and Daichi…

1070
01:01:59,258 --> 01:02:01,218
Kaede wasn't

1071
01:02:01,301 --> 01:02:04,513
just asking him to give her butterflies.

1072
01:02:04,596 --> 01:02:07,307
She wanted a two-way street.

1073
01:02:08,100 --> 01:02:10,477
"I'll put in the effort,
so match my energy,"

1074
01:02:10,561 --> 01:02:12,146
was what she was asking,

1075
01:02:12,229 --> 01:02:13,981
but Daichi misinterpreted it as

1076
01:02:14,064 --> 01:02:16,191
"I need to toughen up so I won't

1077
01:02:16,275 --> 01:02:17,276
let her down."

1078
01:02:17,359 --> 01:02:19,736
He said he'll give her
constant green lights.

1079
01:02:22,448 --> 01:02:24,575
Wow.

1080
01:02:26,785 --> 01:02:27,786
Incredible.

1081
01:02:27,870 --> 01:02:30,664
Props to everyone for
making it through this past month.

1082
01:02:31,331 --> 01:02:34,126
We've had our share of good times,

1083
01:02:34,209 --> 01:02:36,336
and definitely some rough ones too.

1084
01:02:36,420 --> 01:02:40,507
We've built an amazing bond here,
but let's keep fighting.

1085
01:02:40,591 --> 01:02:42,676
Let's give it everything
in this final showdown,

1086
01:02:42,885 --> 01:02:45,846
and hopefully, we all walk away
with a happy ending!

1087
01:02:45,929 --> 01:02:48,557
Cheers!

1088
01:02:49,558 --> 01:02:50,976
Good work.

1089
01:02:51,393 --> 01:02:53,145
Thanks, guys.

1090
01:02:53,520 --> 01:02:55,397
Thank you.

1091
01:02:58,525 --> 01:03:00,694
Let's pull through this last leg.
"Dad Transit".

1092
01:03:02,029 --> 01:03:03,197
Dad Transit.

1093
01:03:05,199 --> 01:03:06,783
Dad Transit?

1094
01:03:07,367 --> 01:03:10,329
Kanako, I've been giving it
100% the whole time.

1095
01:03:11,705 --> 01:03:14,041
Haven't let my guard down
for a single second.

1096
01:03:14,124 --> 01:03:15,709
It's Dad Transit.

1097
01:03:15,792 --> 01:03:17,920
Dad Transit.

1098
01:03:19,880 --> 01:03:21,590
I don't get the vibe.

1099
01:03:21,673 --> 01:03:24,801
I'm too old, I can't get the vibe.

1100
01:03:25,260 --> 01:03:26,678
Alright, let's go around the circle.

1101
01:03:26,762 --> 01:03:28,430
Share one good thing from the trip.

1102
01:03:28,514 --> 01:03:31,391
Hey, I'm Ryo.

1103
01:03:31,475 --> 01:03:33,143
I'm Ryo!

1104
01:03:33,227 --> 01:03:35,020
Thanks guys, seriously.

1105
01:03:35,103 --> 01:03:38,649
Thanks for drinking with me.

1106
01:03:39,525 --> 01:03:44,321
Look, my whole life has been
a total shitshow.

1107
01:03:45,405 --> 01:03:48,575
And…

1108
01:03:48,659 --> 01:03:51,745
I was a complete asshole to X, too.

1109
01:03:54,414 --> 01:03:59,753
Like, I knew I had to change.

1110
01:04:00,337 --> 01:04:03,173
I kept telling myself, I need to change,

1111
01:04:03,257 --> 01:04:06,927
but you don't just transform overnight.

1112
01:04:07,010 --> 01:04:12,182
Still… I figured
I had to face it head-on and fight.

1113
01:04:12,307 --> 01:04:15,477
So I actually gave it a shot.

1114
01:04:15,561 --> 01:04:19,398
Maybe for the first time in my life…

1115
01:04:24,361 --> 01:04:28,323
I actually unlocked my romantic side.

1116
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:31,910
Did you now?

1117
01:04:31,994 --> 01:04:32,828
Congrats!

1118
01:04:32,911 --> 01:04:33,996
That's great!

1119
01:04:34,079 --> 01:04:35,414
Look at you, Ryo!

1120
01:04:35,497 --> 01:04:37,708
Congrats!

1121
01:04:38,292 --> 01:04:39,960
Congrats!

1122
01:04:40,627 --> 01:04:43,839
Ryo's officially unlocked romance mode.

1123
01:04:45,591 --> 01:04:49,720
I've made up my mind.
I'm completely in love with her.

1124
01:04:50,470 --> 01:04:52,556
Don't know if she'll take me,

1125
01:04:52,639 --> 01:04:54,474
but I gotta shoot my shot.

1126
01:04:55,267 --> 01:04:58,228
Everyone else was talking about how much

1127
01:04:58,312 --> 01:05:00,063
they wanted to see their X again,

1128
01:05:00,147 --> 01:05:04,026
but honestly…
I just didn't feel that way at first.

1129
01:05:04,943 --> 01:05:10,866
Eventually, seeing his face each morning
brought me peace.

1130
01:05:11,241 --> 01:05:14,620
I actually found myself missing him.

1131
01:05:15,454 --> 01:05:19,166
Just being able to feel that again
made me happy.

1132
01:05:20,250 --> 01:05:25,339
I was a bit late to the party,
but I had the time of my life.

1133
01:05:31,261 --> 01:05:35,641
Kanako, thank you so much.

1134
01:05:36,266 --> 01:05:39,645
Having you here saved me, seriously.

1135
01:05:40,854 --> 01:05:43,857
You were the most real
and sweet person here.

1136
01:05:44,691 --> 01:05:46,193
Let's hang out again.

1137
01:05:47,944 --> 01:05:51,281
I know I was a total nightmare.

1138
01:05:52,115 --> 01:05:55,452
I acted childishly the entire time.

1139
01:05:57,579 --> 01:06:00,082
So… yeah…

1140
01:06:00,165 --> 01:06:03,001
I'm so sorry.

1141
01:06:03,960 --> 01:06:07,673
So much hit me today.

1142
01:06:13,053 --> 01:06:16,056
I used to say stuff like,
"Re-do my life? Hell no."

1143
01:06:16,139 --> 01:06:19,601
"I wouldn't even want to." But right now…

1144
01:06:19,685 --> 01:06:24,856
I wish I could go back to day one.

1145
01:06:26,817 --> 01:06:31,071
I finally see that
I was the problem all along.

1146
01:06:32,531 --> 01:06:35,033
I see now

1147
01:06:36,076 --> 01:06:40,747
that all the drama was

1148
01:06:40,831 --> 01:06:44,543
actually my fault.

1149
01:06:49,381 --> 01:06:52,843
I'm going to change,

1150
01:06:52,926 --> 01:06:57,305
and the next time you see me,
hopefully, I'll be more mature.

1151
01:06:57,389 --> 01:07:01,101
You will see a more mature Yoko.

1152
01:07:01,977 --> 01:07:03,895
Thank you all so much,

1153
01:07:04,855 --> 01:07:06,690
from the bottom of my heart.

1154
01:07:06,773 --> 01:07:08,775
Meeting you guys was the best thing.

1155
01:07:10,527 --> 01:07:14,406
If I could correct one thing…
this trip wasn't "pain".

1156
01:07:15,615 --> 01:07:17,826
It was "growth".

1157
01:07:19,911 --> 01:07:23,290
I felt like she was telling me,
"It has to be you after all."

1158
01:07:24,750 --> 01:07:28,754
I realized how much pain she was carrying,

1159
01:07:29,171 --> 01:07:32,466
and it broke my heart that
I couldn't hold space for it.

1160
01:07:32,674 --> 01:07:36,553
I felt sorry for her.

1161
01:07:37,012 --> 01:07:40,599
I want to grow alongside her.

1162
01:07:40,682 --> 01:07:45,103
I love her more than words can say.

1163
01:07:49,566 --> 01:07:52,277
Deep down, I think,

1164
01:07:52,360 --> 01:07:55,322
Hiroyoshi still owns most of her heart.

1165
01:07:55,405 --> 01:08:00,160
But I still want to tell her
how I really feel…

1166
01:08:00,869 --> 01:08:05,290
I just want to say "I love you"
one last time.

1167
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:11,755
Just getting to meet
was worth every second.

1168
01:08:11,838 --> 01:08:14,341
This isn't the end.
It's the starting line.

1169
01:08:14,424 --> 01:08:16,510
This is just the beginning.

1170
01:08:16,635 --> 01:08:19,179
Who knows how the confession
will play out,

1171
01:08:21,431 --> 01:08:23,767
but here's to happiness. Say cheers!

1172
01:08:23,850 --> 01:08:26,102
"Say cheers!"

1173
01:08:27,020 --> 01:08:28,647
"Say cheers!"

1174
01:08:29,648 --> 01:08:30,982
"Say cheers!"

1175
01:08:31,233 --> 01:08:32,484
Thank you.

1176
01:08:32,776 --> 01:08:34,069
Let's do this.

1177
01:08:34,736 --> 01:08:35,862
Let's do this!
